## THE GAME-DEV REALITY CHECK

### Scenario 1: 1000 NPCs in a Battle

```cpp
// ============ OPTION A: Pointers Everywhere ============
std::vector<NPC*> npcs;
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    npcs.push_back(new NPC());  // 1000 allocations
}

// Memory layout:
// [ptr1][ptr2][ptr3]... (8KB for pointers)
// [NPC1] (scattered) [NPC2] (scattered) [NPC3] (scattered)
// Total: 1000 allocations → 16KB overhead → cache misses

// ============ OPTION B: References/Vectors ============
std::vector<NPC> npcs;
npcs.reserve(1000);  // ONE allocation
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    npcs.emplace_back();  // Contiguous
}

// Memory layout:
// [NPC1][NPC2][NPC3][NPC4]... (1000 NPCs in a row)
// Total: 1 allocation → 0 overhead → cache hits
```

**Performance difference:**

| Metric | Pointers | Vector (References) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Allocations** | 1000 | 1 |
| **Memory overhead** | 16KB | 0 |
| **Cache misses** | ~50% | ~1% |
| **Iteration speed** | 5ms | 1ms |
| **Memory fragmentation** | Yes | No |

